# tally 2.2.1, 229.2 (L §8.3, §8.4 R-load; OPERATIONS §2.1): the literal-key check is load's in a reality with scenario
# files too: the base's r[2026-01-09] at a range stepped by 7 days from 2026-01-01 refuses the run, LOAD-KEY, before any
# ask, as check does. tally 2.2 made it only inside an answered ask, so qx in sx printed its scenario's line instead.
=== options exit=1
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input r[d in 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 days]: int
input k: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[2026-01-09] = 1 "s"
  r[*] = 0 "s"
  k = 5 "s"

ask q: k
=== sx.tally
scenario sx over t
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version vx
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-02
  replace k = 6 "s"

ask qx: k in sx
=== expect qx
refused: LOAD-KEY 2026-01-09 is not a value of 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 day (m.tally:16)
